# External artifacts (upstream repo clone, HF datasets/adapters, paper PDF) are
# fetched by setup/fetch_external.sh and never committed — the upstream GitHub
# repo has no LICENSE, and the HF payloads are multi-GB.
external/
# Raw sample stores / transcripts (repo-wide *.jsonl rule also applies)
responses/
# Repo-root rules ignore results/ wholesale; re-admit this study's small
# metric artifacts (raw stores stay out via responses/ above).
!results/
results/*
!results/phase0_checks.json
!results/pilot/
results/pilot/*
!results/pilot/20260901T143020Z/
results/pilot/20260901T143020Z/*
!results/pilot/20260901T143020Z/pod/
results/pilot/20260901T143020Z/pod/*
!results/pilot/20260901T143020Z/pod/pilot_summary.json
# Derived artifacts, regenerated by analysis/supervisor.sh every cycle. If they
# are tracked, each regeneration dirties the worktree and launch_pilot.py's
# clean-tree guard then refuses to launch any eval. Final copies are force-added
# at the end of the run.
analysis/all_results.csv
analysis/all_results.json
figures/*_v2.png
